@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1215corr-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1215corr-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapters 12 to 15 corrections"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.6.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1215corr-lineage/1.6.0> ;
    owl:priorVersion <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1215corr-lineage/1.5.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch1215corr_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.6.0 (2026-11-26): Correction of the forecast dates (append, never edit): checkpoint and forecast dates move from 2026-12-07 and 12-08 to 2026-11-28 and 11-29, with the basis read from git. The older dates stay visible in 1.4.0 and 1.5.0."""@en .

ex:CP12_SpecRuns backlog:checkpointDate "2026-11-28T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime .
ex:Obj12_SpecRuns backlog:hasForecastDate "2026-11-28"^^xsd:date ; backlog:hasForecastRationale "Corrected 2026-11-26 10:12 after the Owner's objection that the first dates were too long. The first date (2026-12-07) extrapolated the elapsed days of Lineage10 (three chapters in eight days), but those days were mostly waiting for rulings, an urgency lineage and tool faults, not work. Read from git: a chapter went from spec to released deck and page in about 35 minutes (chapter 11, 2026-11-18), 30 minutes (chapters 11 and 10, 2026-11-24) and about 4 hours (chapter 17, 2026-11-20 13:15 to 17:14); a full page test takes 15 to 20 minutes. Four chapters at the upper figure are about 16 hours of agent work, so the forecast is two days. A forecast, not a deadline." .
